## Self-improvement loop (frontier)

Final scope, what is deliberately out, and open items: `frontier/SCOPE.md`. SurrealDB is native to the
loop (`frontier/surreal.py`): the shared mind is recalled into every agent's context, and accepted work
is distilled into atoms and trajectories as it happens. Short-term memory defaults to SQLite;
`FRONTIER_MIND=off` disables the shared mind, while `FRONTIER_N3=surreal` explicitly selects the
older Surreal short-term backend. The trajectory tool contract is in
`frontier/MIND-TRAJECTORY-DESIGN.md`.

The shared text/trajectory path works for every driver seat. Local tensor
continuation is an optional, model-neutral admission contract in
`frontier/kv_contract.py`; no runtime adapter is admitted yet. TPPE relocation
is a configurable reference in `frontier/tppe_pages.py`, and the exact-prefix
gate is described in `frontier/TPPE-LOCAL-FORWARD-DESIGN.md`. A different causal
prefix invalidates deeper-layer K/V even if a key's position is relocated.

Tensor state belongs to the existing nested SurrealDB substrate. SQLite holds
short-term memory only. `Mind.tensor_exact` now calls the owning Rust runtime
through `native-kv-bridge`, using this mind's existing Surreal endpoint,
namespace, database and workspace. It requires the tensor address to be in the
selected recall. The runtime checks the complete stored page identity and hashes;
raw K/V returns in a bounded binary frame bound to the request. Tensors never
enter a model's text tools. No parallel tensor table or separate store is created.
The model-neutral PLE admission contract also checks complete rosters and finite
values; qualification with a real local forward adapter remains open.
Build and verification instructions: [native-kv-bridge/README.md](native-kv-bridge/README.md).
`Mind.tensor_put` now publishes a single immutable native page through that
same authority and bridge, using raw binary input. The owning PLE-local Rust
store validates dense shape/digests/finite values, selected address/atom linkage,
session identity and lineage receipt. Identical publication is idempotent;
conflicting records are refused without overwrite. The strict disposable test
uses copied production SCHEMAFULL definitions and UNIQUE indexes. Separate
per-layer sessions require distinct request digests under that schema.
Automatic admitted K/V checkpoint export, publication and discovery are
connected through the coordinator described below. Named-state persistence
and production runtime qualification remain open.
Verification: [native publication receipt](reports/native-publication-2026-11-15.md).
`frontier/kv_assembly.py` validates a complete explicit native roster before
reading tensors, assembles contiguous fragments into every layer/head, and
calls the model-neutral runtime gate only after all sizes, hashes and finite
values pass. It rejects inconsistent sessions, missing heads, changed prefixes and
addresses outside the selected recall. Runtime tokenizer/adapter provenance
must come from a trusted export receipt; the native page schema alone does
not attest it. A production local adapter and live forward qualification are
still required.
The same `Mind` exposes `tensor_cache(...)` for complete assembly and
`continue_tensor_cache(...)` for admission and continuation. Native position
version/configuration must match the runtime's `native_position_contract`
digest. These methods require an explicit trusted page roster and opt-in local
runtime; the hosted driver loop continues to use knowledge and memory tools.
Continuation arguments are checked before fetching pages. Runtime output IDs
and generation limits are checked before results are returned to the caller.

`drivers.resolve_local_runtime(seat)` selects an optional runtime plugin from
that driver's `local_runtime` profile entry: `factory` is a Python
`module:callable`, `model_digest` pins the model artifact, and `options` supplies
runtime-specific settings. The factory receives the selected driver model.
There is no built-in model or serving-wire fallback. Layer count, KV head count,
head width, dtype, layout and position contract come from the runtime identity.
The wrapper pins that full identity across export and continuation. Profiles
without this capability keep the shared text/trajectory/SQLite path.
The removed Glimmer-wire experiment is not evidence of support for other
models. No production runtime plugin is qualified yet.

`TensorSpec` is a uniform K/V shorthand. `LayeredTensorSpec` supplies a separate
head count, width, dtype, layout and position contract for each attention layer.
The same nested Surreal tables and Rust bridge assemble heterogeneous layers
from explicit per-layer sessions; no tensor schema or second store is created.
`StateSpec` and `ExactStateSet` also admit named buffers for hybrid/recurrent
state, window-limited attention, counters and opaque packed encodings. The
runtime declares the complete schema; the gate checks it, the causal prefix,
payload sizes and digests before forwarding. Aggregate component/byte budgets
replace a fixed model's layer-count bound. Assembly inspects each fragment once
and reads/verifies its payload bytes; it does not rescan all layers per fragment.

Named state currently supports local export/import admission only: the existing
nested schema can persist rank-two K/V, so recurrent-state persistence fails
before lookup. Extending that owning schema and qualifying independent real
runtimes are still required. Synthetic hybrid continuation and disposable
Surreal heterogeneous-layer tests establish contract behavior, not universal
model or TPPE quality. A plugin must check the active model atomically inside
its forward operation; harness identity checks cannot prevent a server race.
Verification: [model-neutral state receipt](reports/model-neutral-state-2026-11-15.md).

The driver profile now carries its runtime configuration into `agent.ModelClient`.
The pipeline passes its existing shared `Mind`; local requests run through
`frontier/local_chat.py` outside the async event loop. A chat-capable plugin
implements `prepare_chat(messages, tools, mind)`, `generate_tokens(prompt_ids,
max_tokens)`, and `decode_chat(output_ids)`, alongside the exact-state runtime
methods. It owns its tokenizer, chat template and output decoding.

Preparation returns `PreparedChat` with token IDs and optionally a trusted
`NestedPrefix` receipt. PLE checks that receipt's identity and strict causal
prefix, then reads and admits the full native roster through that same `Mind` before
continuing with the remaining token suffix. Without a candidate it generates
locally from the full prompt. Invalid candidates fail locally. Profiles without
`local_runtime` use the existing HTTP client. Native tools and the shared text
tool protocol both work through this dispatch.

For example, a trusted local profile can supply:

```json
{
  "model": "your-selected-model",
  "context": 32768,
  "max_output": 1024,
  "local_runtime": {
    "factory": "your_runtime:create",
    "model_digest": "<64 lowercase SHA-256 hex characters>",
    "bridge": "/absolute/path/to/ple-nested-kv-bridge",
    "options": {}
  }
}
```

This is a plugin contract, not a bundled production adapter. Local generation
currently has a 4,096-token admission limit. The plugin must supply trusted
native page witnesses, or opt into automatic coordination with a typed context.
Completion usage reports the admitted cached-prefix token count; frontier saves
it as `budget.tokens_cached` while total prompt counts remain in `tokens_in`.
These counters do not establish latency, energy or monetary savings.
`PreparedChat(..., context=NativeCacheContext(...))` opts into automatic K/V
checkpoint coordination in `frontier/checkpoints.py`. The context supplies an
existing selected atom address and native geometry/position contracts. PLE
checks eligible power-of-two strict prefixes through exact record metadata
reads, restores the longest complete match, and automatically publishes an
admitted `export_prefix` at the largest eligible anchor after a successful
completion. No hand-built page roster or in-process checkpoint catalog is
needed after a client/database restart. Partial uploads remain misses until
the full expected roster exists; identical retries resume without overwrite.

The record identity binds workspace, model label, weights, tokenizer, adapter,
state schema, native context, prefix digest and fragmentation policy. Native
metadata reads are limited to 128 exact record IDs per request. Anchor hashing
is O(L), candidate count is O(log L), and metadata/payload work scales with the
selected fragments and bytes. No global history scan is used. This does not
prove O(log N) total inference or indexed hyperbolic neighborhood bounds.
The restart gate uses real disk-backed SurrealKV and a synthetic runtime;
trained-model restart/logit quality and performance remain unqualified.
Dispatch verification: [local chat receipt](reports/local-chat-dispatch-2026-11-15.md).
Session continuation: [project handoff](../HANDOFF.md).

Point a model at any folder with a goal and let it work as a long-horizon optimization
engineer. It ports `~/.claude/frontier-loop/frontier_goal.py` (goal, state, cap, complete,
block, pause, resume) into a standalone system. No git, no Docker, no Colima. Any
OpenAI-compatible model can drive: a local MLX server or a hosted API.
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Live cross-harness campaign launcher. Secrets exist only in a mode-600 temp file.
set -euo pipefail
HERE="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
ROOT="${PLE_ROOT:-/Users/stewartbarteau/Desktop/PhyEngLastExam}"
KIT="$ROOT/ple"
TASKS="$ROOT/ple-dev-set/tasks"

if [ -z "${NVIDIA_API_KEY:-}" ]; then
  NVIDIA_API_KEY="$(launchctl getenv NVIDIA_API_KEY 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi
if [ -z "${NVIDIA_API_KEY:-}" ]; then
  NVIDIA_API_KEY="$(security find-internet-password -s https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 -w 2>/dev/null || true)"
fi
: "${NVIDIA_API_KEY:?NVIDIA_API_KEY is absent from environment, launchd, and keychain}"

ENV_FILE="$(mktemp -t ple-ablation-env)"
trap 'rm -f "$ENV_FILE"' EXIT
chmod 600 "$ENV_FILE"
{
  echo "MODEL_API_KEY=$NVIDIA_API_KEY"
  echo "JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1"
  echo "JUDGE_API_KEY=$NVIDIA_API_KEY"
  echo "JUDGE_MODEL=${JUDGE_MODEL:-mistralai/mistral-large-4-1t-a52b}"
} > "$ENV_FILE"

HARNESS="${1:-harness2}"
ACTION="${2:-check}"
MODEL="${MODEL:-mistral}"
case "$HARNESS:$MODEL" in
  harness2:mistral) ENTRY="$("$HERE/scripts/prepare_harness2_entry.sh")" ;;
  *) echo "unsupported campaign cell: $HARNESS:$MODEL" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac

cd "$KIT"
case "$ACTION" in
  check)
    uv run python -m kit check "$ENTRY" --env-file "$ENV_FILE" --no-smoke --work "$HERE/ablations/work/$HARNESS-$MODEL"
    ;;
  run)
    TASK="${3:?usage: run_ablation.sh harness2 run TASK}"
    OUT="$HERE/ablations/runs/$HARNESS/$MODEL/$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
    caffeinate -dimsu uv run python eval/run.py "$ENTRY" --env-file "$ENV_FILE" \
      --tasks-dir "$TASKS" --tasks "$TASK" --trials 1 --attempts 1 --no-export --out "$OUT"
    ;;
  *) echo "action must be check or run" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac

"""Strict, model-neutral admission checks for live ablation receipts."""

from __future__ import annotations

import copy
import datetime as dt
import hashlib
import json
import pathlib
import re
from typing import Any


SHA256 = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{64}$")
ATOM = re.compile(r"^atom:[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$")
TRAJECTORY = re.compile(r"^distilled_trajectory:[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$")


class ReceiptError(ValueError):
    """A receipt is incomplete, incomparable, or not live evidence."""


def _require(mapping: dict[str, Any], keys: tuple[str, ...], where: str) -> None:
    missing = [key for key in keys if key not in mapping]
    if missing:
        raise ReceiptError(f"{where} missing fields: {', '.join(missing)}")


def _timestamp(value: Any, where: str) -> dt.datetime:
    if not isinstance(value, str):
        raise ReceiptError(f"{where} must be an ISO-8601 string")
    try:
        parsed = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError as exc:
        raise ReceiptError(f"{where} is not ISO-8601") from exc
    if parsed.tzinfo is None:
        raise ReceiptError(f"{where} must include a timezone")
    return parsed


def canonical_digest(value: Any) -> str:
    encoded = json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False)
    return hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode()).hexdigest()


def validate_receipt(receipt: dict[str, Any], *, require_mind: bool = True) -> None:
    """Reject anything that cannot enter the final live-results table."""
    _require(receipt, (
        "schema_version", "run_id", "campaign", "harness", "model", "task",
        "seed", "config", "timing", "live", "exit", "judges", "deliverables",
        "calls", "tools", "tokens", "latency", "memory", "process",
        "provider_cost", "unavailable",
    ), "receipt")
    if receipt["schema_version"] != 1:
        raise ReceiptError("unsupported receipt schema")
    for name in ("run_id", "campaign", "task"):
        if not isinstance(receipt[name], str) or not receipt[name].strip():
            raise ReceiptError(f"{name} must be nonempty")

    harness, model = receipt["harness"], receipt["model"]
    if not isinstance(harness, dict) or not isinstance(model, dict):
        raise ReceiptError("harness and model must be objects")
    _require(harness, ("id", "version", "source_digest"), "harness")
    _require(model, ("id", "endpoint_class", "response_ids"), "model")
    if not SHA256.fullmatch(str(harness["source_digest"])):
        raise ReceiptError("harness source_digest must be SHA-256")
    if model["endpoint_class"] not in {"nvidia-api", "local"}:
        raise ReceiptError("unknown endpoint_class")
    if not isinstance(model["response_ids"], list) or not model["response_ids"]:
        raise ReceiptError("live response_ids are required")
    if any(not isinstance(value, str) or not value for value in model["response_ids"]):
        raise ReceiptError("response_ids must be nonempty strings")

    timing = receipt["timing"]
    _require(timing, ("started_at", "ended_at", "wall_seconds"), "timing")
    started = _timestamp(timing["started_at"], "timing.started_at")
    ended = _timestamp(timing["ended_at"], "timing.ended_at")
    if ended < started or not isinstance(timing["wall_seconds"], (int, float)) or timing["wall_seconds"] < 0:
        raise ReceiptError("timing is inconsistent")
    if receipt["live"] is not True:
        raise ReceiptError("scripted, replayed, or simulated runs are inadmissible")

    exit_state = receipt["exit"]
    _require(exit_state, ("state", "unresolved_error", "finish_refusals"), "exit")
    if exit_state["state"] != "complete" or exit_state["unresolved_error"] is not None:
        raise ReceiptError("run did not close cleanly")

    judges = receipt["judges"]
    if not isinstance(judges, list) or not judges:
        raise ReceiptError("at least one judge is required")
    for judge in judges:
        _require(judge, ("id", "passed", "score", "receipt_digest"), "judge")
        if judge["passed"] is not True or not SHA256.fullmatch(str(judge["receipt_digest"])):
            raise ReceiptError("every judge must pass with a receipt digest")

    deliverables = receipt["deliverables"]
    if not isinstance(deliverables, list) or not deliverables:
        raise ReceiptError("deliverable hashes are required")
    for item in deliverables:
        _require(item, ("path", "sha256", "bytes"), "deliverable")
        if not SHA256.fullmatch(str(item["sha256"])) or not isinstance(item["bytes"], int) or item["bytes"] < 0:
            raise ReceiptError("invalid deliverable receipt")

    for name, fields in {
        "calls": ("steps", "retries", "no_progress_turns", "replans"),
        "tools": ("offered", "calls", "successes", "errors", "by_name", "repeated_cycles"),
        "tokens": ("prompt", "output", "cached", "uncached", "max_context"),
        "latency": ("ttft_ms", "e2e_ms", "decode_tokens_per_second"),
        "memory": ("enabled", "recalls", "atom_reads", "minted_atoms", "trajectory_reads", "minted_trajectory", "causal_traces"),
        "process": ("peak_rss_bytes",),
    }.items():
        value = receipt[name]
        if not isinstance(value, dict):
            raise ReceiptError(f"{name} must be an object")
        _require(value, fields, name)
    if receipt["tools"]["calls"] < 1:
        raise ReceiptError("at least one real tool execution is required")

    memory = receipt["memory"]
    if require_mind:
        if not memory["minted_atoms"] or any(not ATOM.fullmatch(str(atom)) for atom in memory["minted_atoms"]):
            raise ReceiptError("validated minted atoms are required")
        if not TRAJECTORY.fullmatch(str(memory["minted_trajectory"])):
            raise ReceiptError("validated minted trajectory is required")
    if receipt["provider_cost"] is None and "provider_cost" not in receipt["unavailable"]:
        raise ReceiptError("unavailable provider cost requires a reason")


def parity_projection(receipt: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:
    """Fields that must be identical across harnesses for one comparison cell."""
    return copy.deepcopy({
        "campaign": receipt.get("campaign"),
        "model": receipt.get("model", {}).get("id"),
        "endpoint_class": receipt.get("model", {}).get("endpoint_class"),
        "task": receipt.get("task"),
        "seed": receipt.get("seed"),
        "config": receipt.get("config"),
    })


def assert_parity(receipts: list[dict[str, Any]]) -> None:
    if len(receipts) < 2:
        raise ReceiptError("parity requires at least two receipts")
    expected = canonical_digest(parity_projection(receipts[0]))
    if any(canonical_digest(parity_projection(receipt)) != expected for receipt in receipts[1:]):
        raise ReceiptError("manifest parity failed")


def assert_mind_ab(off: dict[str, Any], on: dict[str, Any]) -> None:
    """The only configured difference may be the mind flag; on must rescue off."""
    left, right = parity_projection(off), parity_projection(on)
    left_config, right_config = left["config"], right["config"]
    if not isinstance(left_config, dict) or not isinstance(right_config, dict):
        raise ReceiptError("mind A/B config is missing")
    left_config.pop("mind_enabled", None)
    right_config.pop("mind_enabled", None)
    if canonical_digest(left) != canonical_digest(right):
        raise ReceiptError("mind A/B changed fields other than mind availability")
    if off.get("exit", {}).get("state") == "complete" and all(j.get("passed") for j in off.get("judges", [])):
        raise ReceiptError("mind-off run did not fail; this is not a rescue")
    validate_receipt(on, require_mind=True)
    traces = on["memory"]["causal_traces"]
    if not isinstance(traces, list) or not traces:
        raise ReceiptError("mind rescue requires a causal trace")
    for trace in traces:
        _require(trace, ("source_id", "read_step", "action_step", "artifact", "judge_id"), "causal trace")
        if trace["read_step"] >= trace["action_step"]:
            raise ReceiptError("causal source must be read before the influenced action")


def load(path: pathlib.Path) -> dict[str, Any]:
    value = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    if not isinstance(value, dict):
        raise ReceiptError("receipt root must be an object")
    return value

"""Harness2 BenchmarkAdapter that executes against one live PLE task relay."""

from __future__ import annotations

import json
import os
import pathlib
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import tempfile
from typing import Any

from harness2 import config as h2_config
from harness2.benchmarks.jobbench import _render_ctx, render_opencode_tree
from harness2.core.spec import BenchPrompts, BenchSpec, ChannelSpec
from harness2.core import tree
from harness2.substrate.opencode import OpencodeSubstrate


ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
TOOL = ROOT / "bridge" / "ple_tool.py"

BASE_SYSTEM = """You are completing a live Physical Engineering task. Inspect inputs before calculating.
Write a viable deliverable early, verify units and constraints, reopen the final artifact, and finish
with exact paths and remaining limitations. The task filesystem is remote: use
`python scripts/ple_tool.py exec '<command>'`, `read '<path>'`, and
`write '<path>' <local-source-or->`. Never claim a command result before reading its output.
"""

BASE_GUARDRAILS = """Do not inspect tests, graders, answer keys, or rubric files. Do not substitute a
local workspace file for the requested remote deliverable. A finish without a verified remote
deliverable is incomplete. If an approach repeats without new evidence, stop, diagnose, and replan.
"""


def make_base(path: pathlib.Path) -> pathlib.Path:
    surface = OpencodeSubstrate().surface()
    if path.is_dir() and tree.is_tree(surface, path):
        return path
    values = {name: "" for name in surface.always_on}
    values["systemprompt.md"] = BASE_SYSTEM
    values["guardrails.md"] = BASE_GUARDRAILS
    values["tool_descriptions/tool_guidance.md"] = (
        "All task operations go through scripts/ple_tool.py and its authenticated TASK_RELAY_URL.\n"
    )
    values["LongTermMEMORY.md"] = "No task-specific answer is preloaded.\n"
    values["scripts/ple_tool.py"] = TOOL.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
    tree.write_tree(surface, values, path, stubs=True)
    return path


class PleAdapter:
    """A single live PLE task behind Harness2's unchanged method core."""

    def __init__(self, instruction: str, relay_url: str, run_root: pathlib.Path, model: str, timeout: int = 600):
        self.instruction = instruction
        self.relay_url = relay_url
        self.run_root = run_root
        self.model = model
        self.timeout = timeout
        self.task_id = "ple-" + __import__("hashlib").sha256(instruction.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
        self.substrate = OpencodeSubstrate()
        channel = ChannelSpec("opencode", model, effort="high", steps=120, timeout=timeout)
        self.spec = BenchSpec(
            name="ple-live",
            runs_root=run_root,
            install_mode="workspace_agents_md",
            prompts=BenchPrompts(
                work="produce a checked physical-engineering deliverable from a live project workspace",
                domain_word="engineering discipline",
                deliverable_word="engineering deliverable",
                yardstick="Does the trajectory inspect authoritative inputs, calculate reproducibly, write the requested artifact, and verify it?",
                selection_checks="Prefer complete verified artifacts, traceable calculations, correct units, and explicit assumptions.",
            ),
            channels={"proposer": channel, "selector": channel},
            state_deliverable=True,
            obs_trunc=50_000,
        )
        self._base = make_base(run_root / "base-harness")

    def tasks(self, split: str = "all") -> list[str]:
        return [self.task_id]

    def domain_of(self, task_id: str) -> str:
        self._check_task(task_id)
        return "physical-engineering"

    def task_prompt(self, task_id: str) -> str:
        self._check_task(task_id)
        return self.instruction

    def task_files(self, task_id: str) -> None:
        self._check_task(task_id)
        return None

    def base_harness(self) -> pathlib.Path:
        return self._base

    def validate_tree(self, value: tree.Tree) -> None:
        joined = "\n".join(value.values())
        if "ple_tool.py" not in joined or "TASK_RELAY_URL" not in joined:
            raise ValueError("PLE harness tree must retain the authenticated relay tool guidance")

    def execute(self, task_id: str, harness_dir: pathlib.Path | None, run_id: str, *, timeout: int | None = None) -> pathlib.Path:
        self._check_task(task_id)
        run_dir = self.run_root / "executions" / re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]+", "_", run_id)
        if (run_dir / "closed.json").is_file():
            return run_dir
        shutil.rmtree(run_dir, ignore_errors=True)
        workspace = run_dir / "workspace"
        workspace.mkdir(parents=True)
        render_opencode_tree(pathlib.Path(harness_dir or self._base), workspace, _render_ctx("physical engineering"))
        (workspace / "scripts").mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copy2(TOOL, workspace / "scripts" / "ple_tool.py")
        prompt = (
            "Complete the live task below. The actual project filesystem is available only through "
            "scripts/ple_tool.py; local files are harness support, not deliverables.\n\n" + self.instruction
        )
        stream = run_dir / "events.jsonl"
        log = run_dir / "stderr.log"
        command = [
            str(h2_config.BUN), "run", "--cwd", str(h2_config.OPENCODE_DIR / "packages" / "opencode"),
            "--conditions=browser", "src/index.ts", "run", prompt, "--dir", str(workspace),
            "--model", self.model, "--variant", "high", "--format", "json",
        ]
        env = h2_config.scrub_env(keep=h2_config.provider_keys(self.model))
        env.update({
            "TASK_RELAY_URL": self.relay_url,
            "NO_PROXY": "127.0.0.1,localhost," + env.get("NO_PROXY", ""),
            "no_proxy": "127.0.0.1,localhost," + env.get("no_proxy", ""),
            "OPENCODE_EXPERIMENTAL_OUTPUT_TOKEN_MAX": os.environ.get("MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS", "16000"),
            "OPENCODE_PERMISSION": json.dumps({"external_directory": {"*": "deny", f"{workspace}/**": "allow"}}),
            "XDG_DATA_HOME": str(workspace / ".ocdata"),
            "XDG_STATE_HOME": str(workspace / ".ocstate"),
        })
        with stream.open("w", encoding="utf-8") as out, log.open("w", encoding="utf-8") as err:
            result = subprocess.run(command, cwd=workspace, env=env, text=True, stdout=out, stderr=err, timeout=timeout or self.timeout)
        if result.returncode != 0:
            raise RuntimeError(f"OpenCode exited {result.returncode}; see {log}")
        if not stream.stat().st_size:
            raise RuntimeError("OpenCode returned no trajectory")
        (run_dir / "closed.json").write_text(json.dumps({"returncode": 0}) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
        return run_dir

    def delivered(self, run_dir: pathlib.Path) -> bool:
        return (pathlib.Path(run_dir) / "closed.json").is_file()

    def trajectory(self, run_dir: pathlib.Path, *, obs_trunc: int) -> str:
        return self.substrate.read_trajectory(pathlib.Path(run_dir) / "events.jsonl", obs_trunc=obs_trunc, max_chars=200_000)

    def deliverable_text(self, run_dir: pathlib.Path) -> str:
        return self.trajectory(run_dir, obs_trunc=self.spec.obs_trunc)

    def deliverable_files(self, run_dir: pathlib.Path) -> dict[str, str]:
        return {"trajectory.md": self.deliverable_text(run_dir)}

    def score(self, run_dir: pathlib.Path, task_id: str) -> None:
        self._check_task(task_id)
        return None

    def _check_task(self, task_id: str) -> None:
        if task_id != self.task_id:
            raise ValueError(f"unknown live task {task_id!r}")

"""PLE serve-protocol entry point using Google's pinned Harness2 method."""

from __future__ import annotations

import asyncio
import hashlib
import json
import os
import pathlib

import taskbridge


ROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent


def _configure() -> str:
    model = os.environ.get("MODEL_NAME", "")
    base = os.environ.get("MODEL_BASE_URL", "")
    key = os.environ.get("MODEL_API_KEY", "")
    if not model or not base or not key:
        raise RuntimeError("MODEL_NAME, MODEL_BASE_URL, and MODEL_API_KEY are required")
    routed = model if "/" in model and model.split("/", 1)[0] in {"openai", "nvidia"} else f"openai/{model}"
    os.environ.update({
        "OPENAI_API_KEY": key,
        "OPENAI_BASE_URL": base,
        "HARNESS2_SOLVER_MODEL": routed,
        "HARNESS2_IMPROVER_MODEL": routed,
        "HARNESS2_JUDGE_MODEL": model,
        "HARNESS2_JUDGE_BASE_URL": base,
        "HARNESS2_JUDGE_API_KEY": key,
    })
    return routed


async def solve(session: taskbridge.Session) -> str:
    model = _configure()
    from harness2.core import schedule
    from harness2.core.proposer import Proposer
    from ablations.harness2_ple import PleAdapter

    digest = hashlib.sha256(session.instruction.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
    run_root = ROOT / "ablations" / "runs" / "harness2" / model.replace("/", "__") / digest
    run_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    remaining = session.time_left() or 3600
    per_call = max(120, min(900, int(max(120, remaining - 180) / 7)))
    async with taskbridge.Relay(session) as relay:
        adapter = PleAdapter(session.instruction, relay.url, run_root, model, timeout=per_call)
        proposer = Proposer(adapter.spec.channels["proposer"], audit_dir=run_root / "audit", attempts=2)
        result = await asyncio.to_thread(
            schedule.run_task,
            adapter.task_id,
            1,
            adapter=adapter,
            prop=proposer,
            runs_root=run_root / "adapt",
            modes=("agg",),
            seed=20261115,
            pool_policy="finals",
        )
    record = result.to_dict()
    (run_root / "harness2-result.json").write_text(json.dumps(record, indent=2) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
    selection = record.get("selections", {}).get("agg", {})
    if record.get("status") != "ok" or not selection.get("chosen_run_dir"):
        raise RuntimeError(f"Harness2 did not close the task: {record.get('errors')}")
    return "Harness2 completed Propose-Probe-Compose; adopted live run " + str(selection["chosen_label"])


if __name__ == "__main__":
    # Harness2 is pinned under this tree and never imported from a global install.
    import sys
    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / "ablations" / "vendor" / "harness2"))
    taskbridge.run(solve)


