ablations/vendor/deepseek-harness/docs/upgrade-guide/v0.2.2-alpha.2/pi-ai-request-image-count/guide.md:12:`llm-pi-ai` previously bounded request images only by `maxRequestImageBytes`, so every retained image was resent until that byte bound was reached. Each provider route now also has `maxRequestImages` (default 50) and `imageOffloadCountQuantum` (default 10). When a request carries more retained images than `maxRequestImages`, `dsh-compaction-image-offload` replaces the oldest `imageOffloadCountQuantum` images with placeholder text and retries. The omission is recorded in the Session and does not revert. This affects Sessions with more than 50 images on any pi-ai route, including providers that accept more images per request.
