ablations/vendor/deepseek-harness/packages/experimental/forge-session/README.md:41:Numeric `gh pr view`, `edit`, and `checkout` selectors accept `--repo OWNER/REPO`, `--repo=OWNER/REPO`, and `-R OWNER/REPO` in either argument order. A repository containing its host, or a literal `GH_HOST` assignment, supplies a URL directly. For a single command, optionally piped through `head`, `tail`, or `cat`, a completed foreground Bash call without a host runs a read-only `gh pr view <number> --repo <repository> --json url` through the same shell service, cwd, literal environment assignments, managed environment, and standing sandbox policy. The CLI resolves its configured host. A successful lookup appends a `reference` binding record; failures leave bindings unchanged and log a warning. A Bash call inside a PTC program runs its lookup after the enclosing root call settles, so the lookup follows that root call's cancellation. This live observer requires `tools`, `shell`, and `shellEnv`; projection-only compositions still recover recorded URLs. Queries share `discoveryTimeoutMs`, stop on caller cancellation, and are aborted and awaited on service disposal.
