            "content": "exit_code=0\n########## project/00_admin/T-204_Document_Transmittal.pdf 1\n== PAGE 1\nT-204 Document Transmittal\npage 1\nDocument Transmittal T-204\nNorthern Divide Data Campus, Building A2 \u00b7 to the delegated engineer \u00b7 20 August 2026\nThe documents below are issued for the roof diaphragm and shear wall package. Items marked superseded are in the\nproject archive and must not be designed to.\nitem\ndocument\nrevision\ndate\nstatus\nNote 1 EOR-NDDC-A2-S01 Structural Design Criteria\n2\n2026-08-14\nissued\nNote 2 WT-2026-07 Boundary Layer Wind Study\nfinal\n2026-07-22\nissued\nNote 3 WT-2026-07 pressure coefficient data file\nfinal\n2026-07-22\nissued\nNote 4 TS-2026-02 Topographic Wind Study\nfinal\n2026-04-30\nissued\nNote 5 NDDC-A2 Federated Model (IFC)\n2026-08\n2026-08-09\nissued\nNote 6 SR-2026-118 Roof Line Scan Report\n1\n2026-08-18\nissued\nNote 7 A-101 Roof Plan\nC\n2026-06-05\nissued\nNote 8 A-301 Exterior Elevations\nC\n2026-06-05\nissued\nNote 9 S-201 Roof Framing Plan\nC\n2026-06-19\nissued\n10\nPC-S01 Precast Panel Schedule\n2024-11\n2024-11-08\nfor information; superseded by the federated model\n11\nPC-S02 Precast Panel Elevations\n2\n2026-05-12\nissued\n12\nEOR-NDDC-A2-S01 Structural Design Criteria\n0\n2024-05-03\nsuperseded - archive only\n13\nA-101 Roof Plan\nA\n2024-03-19\nsuperseded - archive only\n14\nPC-S02 Precast Panel Elevations\n1\n2024-10-02\nsuperseded - archive only\n15\nHall B Lateral Study (Building A1)\n-\n2023-09-14\nanother building, for information only\n\n########## project/00_admin/Spec_01_33_00_Submittal_Procedures.pdf 2\n== PAGE 1\nSpec 01 33 00 Submittal Procedures\npage 1\nSection 01 33 00 - Submittal Procedures\nNorthern Divide Data Campus, Building A2 \u00b7 issued for construction \u00b7 14 August 2026\n1.1 Summary\nThis section governs the form of delegated-design submittals.\n1.2 Units\nFeet and inches, kips and pounds. Distributed loads and diaphragm unit shears in pounds per linear foot (plf);\nconcentrated forces and reactions in kips; deflections in inches; costs in United States dollars.\n1.3 Coordinates\nPlan coordinates are on the building grid with its origin at the south-west building corner, X positive east, Y positive\nnorth, in feet.\n1.4 Transmittal\nOne compressed archive per submittal.\n1.5 Schedules\nSchedules are delivered as a single workbook, one worksheet per schedule, the first row of each worksheet being the\ncolumn headings named in the design criteria and in the issued templates. Every row is complete: a cell left blank, or\nfilled with a placeholder such as TBD or N/A, makes the schedule incomplete and it is returned.\n1.6 Calculation package and design basis\nCalculations are delivered as one PDF on 8-1/2 x 11 portrait sheets covering the sections the design criteria lists, with a\nseparate design basis narrative in Markdown. The design basis carries a table of the values the design was built\non, one per row, in the form\n    | item | value | source |\nusing exactly these item names:\nitem\nwhat it states\nKzt\ntopographic factor used\nKe\nground elevation factor used\nq_h_psf\nvelocity pressure at mean roof height\nscreen_wall_top_ft\ntop elevation of the mechanical screen wall\nasbuilt_opening_panel\npanel mark(s) whose as-built opening is not on the 2024 precast shop drawing\nasd_combination\nthe load combination the reported loads are on\nomega_d\nthe deck catalogue's safety factor for ASD capacity\nanalysis_method\nthe diaphragm idealisation used\nmesh_level\nthe refinement level the reported quantities are taken at\nand, below that table, a second table of the governing wind scenario for each wall line, one row per line, in the form\n    | line | governing scenario |\n    | S    | W05                |\nThe narrative also records, in prose, every conflict between issued documents that the engineer resolved, and how.\n1.7 Drawings\nPlan view drawings are delivered as DXF on the building grid in feet. The drawing carries the layers\n\n== PAGE 2\nSpec 01 33 00 Submittal Procedures\npage 2\n    S-DIAP-SHEAR\n    S-DIAP-ZONE\n    S-WALL-REAC\n    S-CHRD\n    S-COLL\n    S-ANNO-TEXT\n    S-GRID\nwith the diaphragm unit shear distribution on S-DIAP-SHEAR, the deck zone boundaries on S-DIAP-ZONE, the shear\nwall reactions on S-WALL-REAC, chords on S-CHRD, collectors on S-COLL, the building grid on S-GRID and all\nannotation on S-ANNO-TEXT. Both the TRANSVERSE and the LONGITUDINAL direction are drawn, each labelled\nwith that word, and the drawing states on its face that the loads shown are ASD.\n1.8 Constraint register\nEvery submittal carries a register of the requirements the design was engineered to, one row per requirement, as a\nworkbook with a worksheet named Register and the columns document, clause, requirement, value, units, items.\n\n"
